out/
_out/

# `boards/*/bsp/out/` was here until RFCT-343 moved every BSP build product to
# `_out/boards/<board>/`, where `_out/` above already covers it. It is REMOVED
# rather than left as a tombstone, and the two tombstones further down are why
# that is the right call for this one and not for those: `.devkeys/` and `/ca/`
# stay because a stale directory at either path holds a PRIVATE KEY, and an
# absent-minded `git add -A` on a developer machine that still has one would
# publish it. A stale `boards/<b>/bsp/out/` holds a kernel image and a U-Boot
# binary -- public build products -- and `out/` on the first line matches a
# directory of that name at any depth, so a leftover from before the move is
# still not committable by accident. Nothing is protected by keeping the line,
# and a rule naming a path the build no longer writes is one a reader has to
# check before trusting.

# Development TUF signing keys, generated by `rauc-sign gen-dev-keys`.
# Key material is never committed.
# Retired dev-key location: the trust root moved to /ca/, but stale
# .devkeys dirs (holding a private CA key) still exist on dev machines.
pkgs/rauc/.devkeys/
pkgs/rauc-sign/.devkeys/

# Everything a release needs to be configured and signed: the RAUC CA and its
# signer (meta/rauc/), the update configuration and the package signing key
# (meta/updates/), and the GENERATED marker. It is either production material
# an operator put there or a development-grade one pkgs/rauc/gen-dev-keys.sh
# generated (marked by meta/GENERATED). Neither is ever committed: a committed
# signing key would make every device trust anything anyone builds, and a
# committed production CA cert would let this repository history decide what
# the fleet trusts. meta.example/ is the committed statement of the shape.
/meta/

# Retired trust-root location: PLAN-070 absorbed ca/ into meta/rauc/. The entry
# stays as a TOMBSTONE, exactly as pkgs/rauc/.devkeys/ above does, because a
# stale ca/ on a developer machine still holds a private CA key and this is
# what stops an absent-minded `git add -A` committing it after the move.
/ca/

# The RAUC system configuration is RENDERED from pkgs/rauc/system.conf.in and
# boards/cx3576/board.env by pkgs/rauc/render-config.sh, which rootfs/build.sh
# runs before staging the overlay. It is generated rather than committed so the
# template stays the single source of truth and the rendered file cannot drift
# away from it.
rootfs/overlay/etc/rauc/system.conf

# The image's RAUC keyring is STAGED from meta/rauc/ by rootfs/build.sh, which
# refuses one found in the overlay -- the overlay is not a source of trust.
# The entry stays so that a copy left over from before that rule can never be
# committed into the one directory the build copies wholesale into the image.
rootfs/overlay/etc/rauc/keyring.pem

# Built by pkgs/rauc/build.sh, like pkgs/podman/out-*: compiled artefacts, not source.
pkgs/rauc/out-*/
pkgs/rauc/versions.lock

# Repository-local scratch, shared with containers as a bind-mount root. All
# throwaway compile, verify and container-exchange paths belong here.
#
# NOT the system /tmp: the docker daemon does not share this session's /tmp, so
# a bind mount of it succeeds and delivers an empty directory. Named tmp/ and
# not runtime/ because a real runtime directory would then be silently ignored,
# and because the harness measurements quote paths like /srv/bkd/runtime/bun
# that have nothing to do with this one.
tmp/
